# Environment: torch-firered
#
# PyTorch for the `firered` stack alone. It is its own environment because FireRed pins
# transformers exactly at 5.1.0, which no other package here can accept: mlx-audio 0.4.5
# requires >=5.5.0,<5.13.0 and VibeVoice requires >=4.51.3,<5.0.0. The resolver's own
# messages for all ten conflicting groupings are recorded in
# model_tests/benchmark/results/2026-08-17-environment-partition.json.
#
# Serves the packages: firered-asr2s (which supplies the vad, lid, asr, and punctuator roles).
#
# Citation: model_tests/firered/FireRedASR2S/pyproject.toml on a clean checkout at 4e7d9aa,
# which matches the as-built venv that produced every recorded FireRed figure.
#
# Do not lock from that checkout's requirements.txt. It pins torch==2.1.0+cu118 and
# transformers==4.51.3 against a CUDA index, cannot be what ran on Apple Silicon, and
# disagrees with both the pyproject and the installed environment. Upstream ships two
# contradictory dependency files; only one of them describes the recorded runs.
#
# kaldi_native_fbank is here because fireredasr2s/fireredlid/data/feat.py:7 imports it and
# **no** upstream dependency list declares it — pyproject.toml omits it entirely. Without it
# the LID stage fails at import time on an otherwise correctly provisioned environment.
# 1.22.3 is the as-built version.
#
# The FireRedASR2S package itself is not listed: it is a pinned source checkout installed
# with --no-deps, so this file holds only its third-party dependencies.
#
# Python: 3.12.12, the as-built version.
torch==2.10.0
torchaudio==2.10.0
transformers==5.1.0
numpy==2.4.2
cn2an==0.5.23
kaldiio==2.18.1
kaldi_native_fbank==1.22.3
sentencepiece==0.2.1
soundfile==0.13.1
textgrid==1.6.1
